// <auto-generated>ANG: the noise waves (world.noise_waves, combat-play/noise-waves). The client only draws: Go says which sounds the hero hears and how far each carries, the numbers of the look are data (PocConfig).
// One mesh per floor of a wave, one small texture of the plan cells per mesh, drawn by one render pass after the post-processing: the scene's HDR exposure is not the screen's, and the approved numbers are the screen's.
// A blow starts at its contact frame, not when the event came, so the ring leaves the hand that struck.
// The clock is the show's own (CombatNow): it stops when the world is paused and follows a slow-motion review.
// Seen only in the tactical view (owner 04.11, world.tactical_mode): a view, not a rule, off by default, not in a save. The server publishes the same either way; with the view off nothing is drawn.
// `--poc-noise-measure <dir>` (review only): at sampled frames renders the camera twice, with and without the waves, and writes the difference and the camera for the measure of the radius and the brightness.
